{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Gt9Mejmv4ZDsQr6Tq3urpN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a personal productivity + R&D control system built for J.C. Liechty. Grounded summary:\n\n**What it is**\n- A single-folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`), stdlib-only Python application â€” no database, no external dependencies (one declared exception: optional `pywinpty` for terminals). Plain markdown files are the source of truth.\n- Ships as a **persistent local web server** (`anchor_gui.py`, bound to `http://localhost:8777`) run by the Windows NSSM service `anchor`. It generates the full dashboard HTML on every request and writes changes directly back to markdown.\n\n**Core purpose â€” task/project management**\n- A daily dashboard for tracking tasks across life domains (academic, commercial, family, writing). Tasks move through a lifecycle: Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored, stored in markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `domains/*.md`, `INBOX.md`, `CANCELLED.md`, etc.).\n- Fully interactive in the browser (check off, add, edit, capture) plus a parallel CLI engine (`anchor.py`) mirroring the same logic and generating a static `dashboard.html`.\n- A daily self-test (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) runs at 5 AM via Task Scheduler, verifying file integrity and exercising every endpoint and the R&D surfaces (all model calls stubbed).\n\n**The R&D \"Project Cockpit\" surface (its major built-out feature)**\n- Turns each project into a mission-control \"cockpit\" for the **trio workflow**: researchPrime (Research) â†’ Crucible (Planning) â†’ Foreman (Build).\n- Each lane shows its most-recent session as a **tile with a status light** (green=working, amber=needs-you, red=crashed, grey=idle/done); clicking expands an **inline panel** with a cached summary on top and a **real ConPTY terminal** (xterm.js) below.\n- Sessions are durable, isolated server-side terminals â€” each gets its own git worktree/branch; they survive disconnect and are managed like windows (open/attach/minimize/kill).\n- Additional capabilities: an engine toggle (Claude â†” Gemini, Gemini research-only), per-lane document roles, project cost/tokens/time rollups, a grass-catcher idea board with promote-to-lane, stage handoffs between planning and build, and type-aware deliverable launching (skill/tool/service/program/doc).\n- Branded as a **Ghost World Labs** tool \"powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢.\"\n\n**Status**: v4 \"Project Cockpit\" is built (9 waves green) and merged to master, with a v4.1 clean rebuild of the project-window render (merge `37f59b3`).\n\nOne caveat on grounding: this summary is drawn from the project's `CLAUDE.md` and design memories rather than a fresh read of the code itself â€” I can verify any specific claim against the source if you want."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45832,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b6543ecf-53d6-4aba-aed6-d70637278c00","uuid":"0e44d934-8d41-45ee-bde9-1a44e0f7e09f","request_id":"req_011Cc2JUtSLEazorf5MSGDQX"}
